        <headline>Flood Advisory issued September 25 at 3:41PM MDT until September 25 at 5:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.

* WHERE...West Central Jefferson County in central Colorado...

* WHEN...Until 545 PM MDT.

* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...

- At 341 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin
shortly in the advisory area. Up to 1 inch of rain has fallen.

- This includes the following streams and drainages...
Troublesome Creek, Cub Creek, Bear Creek, North Turkey Creek,
Blue Creek and Bergen Creek. Additional rainfall amounts up to
0.5 inches are expected over the area. This additional rain will
result in minor flooding.

- Some locations that will experience flooding include...
Evergreen, Kittredge and Wah Keeney Park.
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
